# Gameplay cleanup on menu

ProjectContext models and Global services survive scene unloads. After Leave (or any transition into `MenuGameFlowState`) every gameplay system must drop match state. Entering `SessionGameFlowState` must start from scratch, not reuse leftover objects or fields.

Implement `IGameplaySession` on the owning service (not the model). Bind so Zenject collects it (`BindInterfacesTo` / `BindInterfacesAndSelfTo`). `GameplaySessionLifecycle` calls `CleanupGameplay` on menu and `RestartGameplay` on session.

```csharp
// BAD — look pivot stays parented to a destroyed player after Leave
public override void OnStopLocalPlayer() { }

// GOOD — service tears down runtime and resets the model
public sealed class GameCameraService : IGameCameraService, IGameplaySession {
    public void CleanupGameplay() {
        TearDownCameras();
        _model.Clear();
        SpawnIdleCameras();
    }

    public void RestartGameplay() => CleanupGameplay();
}
```

- Cleanup is idempotent. Destroy `DontDestroyOnLoad` gameplay objects; do not keep destroyed Transform refs
- Models only store state; the service resets them (`Clear` / `ResetMatch`)
- Do not rely on scene unload alone. Players, cameras, and spawn flags live in Global / DDOL
